.TH PDF-PAGE-MERGER 1 "2026-10-25" "pdf-page-merger 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdf-page-merger \- merge PDF files and reorder pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdf-page-merger
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdf-page-merger
is a desktop application for combining multiple PDF files into one
document.  Pages from every input file are shown as thumbnails; drag a
thumbnail to change its position in the final document.
.PP
Encrypted PDFs are unlocked per file.  Passwords are kept in memory
only.  When an encrypted file is unlocked, a temporary unencrypted copy
is created in a private temporary directory for thumbnail rendering and
merging.  The original files are never modified.
.PP
The merged PDF is written to a temporary file and atomically moved into
place after the whole document has been generated.  The result is not
encrypted.
.SH OPTIONS
The application does not define command line options.  Each non-option
argument that ends in
.B .pdf
is opened in the initial page list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Standard Qt platform selector.  Set it to
.B offscreen
for automated/headless smoke tests.
.TP
.B QT_SCALE_FACTOR
Standard Qt scaling override for high-DPI displays.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/pdf-page-merger-*
Private working directory containing decrypted working copies and
thumbnails for the current session.  It is removed on a normal exit.
.SH NOTES
Bookmarks, form fields, attachments, and digital signatures are not
guaranteed to be preserved in the merged output.  Page content, page
size, and page rotation are retained.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B non-zero
The application failed to start, or Python raised an unhandled error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1),
.BR pdftoppm (1),
.BR qpdf (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Local Package Builder
